%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cfea244e7fd483e40b8c5da0774d99b3, type: 3}
  m_Name: ModelsScriptable
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  models:
  - sfx: motherboard
    modelName: 'Motherboard '
    modelVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4bbb7cc1ad3173b4e82cb72ecc34f27e, type: 3}
    description: The primary circuit board in a computer, the Motherboard, connects
      essential components like the CPU, RAM, storage, and peripherals, enabling
      communication and overall functionality. It also includes expansion slots,
      ports, and chipsets to support additional hardware
  - sfx: cpu
    modelName: 'Central Processing Unit (CPU) '
    modelVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 2015f6df3b9b4584fa6a28a63fd0e119, type: 3}
    description: 'The CPU, or processor, is the computer''s "brain," responsible
      for executing program instructions through arithmetic, logic, control, and
      input/output operations. It processes data, manages tasks, and coordinates
      with other hardware for smooth system performance.

'
  - sfx: hdd
    modelName: Hard Disk Drive (HDD)
    modelVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: dd4ab8fbc1f2d9448b6e2dc350001c01, type: 3}
    description: An HDD is the main storage device in a computer, storing the operating
      system, applications, and user data. Unlike RAM, it retains data permanently
      using spinning magnetic disks to read and write information.
  - sfx: opticDisk
    modelName: 'Optical Disk Drive (ODD) '
    modelVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: be06fd06b9e0f6044b186fa4630b0877, type: 3}
    description: 'Optical Disk Drive is a hardware component that reads and writes
      data from optical discs such as CDs, DVDs, and Blu-ray discs using laser technology.
      It allows users to install software, watch movies, listen to music, and back
      up data.

'
  - sfx: powerSupply
    modelName: 'Power Supply Unit (PSU) '
    modelVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1d6c28c1abeddb2418d03dfd8423b4c8, type: 3}
    description: 'The Power Supply Unit (PSU) converts high-voltage AC from a wall
      outlet into low-voltage DC for the motherboard and other components. It ensures
      stable power delivery and supports efficient operation based on the system''s
      wattage needs.

'
  - sfx: fan
    modelName: CPU fan
    modelVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: fb738a7bb37c71a47aa12fdc3f1138db, type: 3}
    description: 'A CPU Fan is a cooling component that dissipates heat from the
      processor, preventing overheating and ensuring stable performance by maintaining
      optimal temperatures through airflow.

'
  - sfx: ram
    modelName: Random Access Memory (RAM)
    modelVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 696b0dd2ce9f434408ddac79b4e2700e, type: 3}
    description: 'RAM is a high-speed, volatile memory that temporarily stores data
      and instructions the CPU needs for immediate tasks. It enables quick access
      and efficient multitasking, boosting system performance compared to long-term
      storage like hard drives or SSDs.

'
  - sfx: 24pin
    modelName: 20/24-pin ATX Main Power Connector
    modelVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cec7a3f72d63fcd4c991c5ca96d23265, type: 3}
    description: 'The 24-pin ATX power connector links the power supply to the motherboard,
      delivering essential voltage for system operation. Older systems use 20 pins,
      while modern ones require all 24, with some PSUs offering detachable extra
      pins for compatibility.

'
  - sfx: 4x4pin
    modelName: ATX12V Power Connector
    modelVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ed92a114fb1568f4c8011b163cac5e01, type: 3}
    description: 'The ATX12V Power Connector supplies dedicated 12V power to the
      CPU, ensuring stable energy delivery for consistent performance and preventing
      voltage drops, especially in high-power systems.

'
  - sfx: sata
    modelName: Serial ATA Connectors
    modelVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c31b74387460ea842a0dae0c7a9ac1d5, type: 3}
    description: SATA connectors, with a 7-pin design, enable high-speed data transfer
      between the motherboard and storage devices like HDDs and SSDs. Using dedicated
      cables, they support data rates up to 6.0 Gb/s for reliable performance.
  - sfx: frontPanel
    modelName: 'System Panel Connector  '
    modelVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 231027599236b4c47829567c16bf1910, type: 3}
    description: 'The System Panel Connector links the motherboard to case controls
      like the power button, reset button, and LED indicators. Proper wiring ensures
      these functions work correctly for system operation and monitoring.

'
